1
00:00:02,634 --> 00:00:04,174
(Raj:)It's, like,
the best one they make,

2
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:06,271
(Raj:)I just can't get it to work.
I'll figure it out.

3
00:00:06,273 --> 00:00:09,843
(Raj:)It streams HD video straight
to your phone while it's flying.

4
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:11,174
(Howard:)Nice.

5
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:13,278
(Howard:)Where were you
when I was single?

6
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,986
(Leonard:)Okay, we should leave in
about an hour. You all packed?

7
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:21,156
(Penny:)Uh, yeah, I just need to throw
in a few last minute things--

8
00:00:21,155 --> 00:00:23,255
(Penny:)you know, makeup,
underwear, clothes.

9
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,894
(Sheldon:)If your bathroom floor

10
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:27,963
(Sheldon:)counts as a carry-on,
you're packed.

11
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:30,532
(Amy:)Leonard,
have you ever given

12
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:31,901
(Amy:)a high school
commencement speech before?

13
00:00:31,899 --> 00:00:33,869
(Leonard:)Nope. It's pretty exciting.

14
00:00:33,868 --> 00:00:36,038
(Sheldon:)Aren't you afraid
of being blinded?

15
00:00:36,037 --> 00:00:38,007
(Leonard:)How would I be blinded?

16
00:00:38,005 --> 00:00:39,675
(Sheldon:)At the end of the ceremony,

17
00:00:39,673 --> 00:00:42,073
(Sheldon:)all the students throw
those pointy hats in the air.

18
00:00:43,343 --> 00:00:44,913
(Sheldon:)It's all pomp and circumstance

19
00:00:44,912 --> 00:00:47,342
(Sheldon:)until someone loses an eye.

20
00:00:47,348 --> 00:00:48,918
(Leonard:)I'll take my chances.

21
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:50,186
(Sheldon:)Fine.

22
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:51,584
(Sheldon:)I wonder if they make

23
00:00:51,585 --> 00:00:53,615
"I told you so"
cards in braille.

24
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,185
(Raj:)Look, the problem
with commencement speeches

25
00:00:57,191 --> 00:00:59,261
(Raj:)is that they're boring.

26
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,430
(Raj:)Ooh, do you own
a T-shirt cannon?

27
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,365
(Howard:)Why would he own
a T-shirt cannon?

28
00:01:04,365 --> 00:01:06,395
(Raj:)I don't know. Why do I own one?

29
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,000
(Amy:)I think it's really nice

30
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:10,503
(Amy:)that you're sharing
this experience with Penny.

31
00:01:10,504 --> 00:01:12,174
(Leonard:)Mm, I thought
it'd be fun

32
00:01:12,173 --> 00:01:14,003
(Leonard:)to show her my old
stomping grounds.

33
00:01:14,008 --> 00:01:17,078
(Leonard:)I even know the exact spot
where they used to stomp me.

34
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,608
(Bernadette:)Well, now you
get to go back

35
00:01:19,613 --> 00:01:21,013
(Bernadette:)as a successful
scientist.

36
00:01:21,015 --> 00:01:23,045
(Amy:)With a beautiful girl
on your arm.

37
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:26,020
(Sheldon:)And a pointy hat sticking
out of your eyeball.

